  "body": "## What changed\n\nOpposite D5 by 8 mm holes across a 50 mm span stay separate.\nDetection preserves each hole's mouth, inward direction, and blind depth.\nIt reports directed findings on mills through the existing detection command.\nExisting generation checks still refuse unsupported drilling directions.\n\nThe recognition helpers now live in separate modules.\nThe recognition source files stay below 400 lines.\n\n## Cause\n\nBoth merge loops compared transverse centers without checking axial separation.\nThe output always placed the mouth at the highest coordinate.\nMill detection also discarded all radial findings.\n\nReadings: the drilling recognition, hole record, and cross-cycle modules; the app material and generation paths.\nThe held tests in `ce2747ca1` supplied the reduced closed-block fixture.\n\n## Tests\n\nThese pins failed before the fix and passed after it:\n\n- `opposite_blind_z_walls_keep_their_separate_depths`\n- `opposite_blind_radial_walls_keep_their_separate_depths`\n- `opposite_blind_radial_holes_enter_from_their_own_mouths`\n- `six_blind_holes_on_a_d50_bar_keep_their_depths_and_mouths`\n- `mill_detection_preserves_opposite_blind_radial_holes_and_refuses_generation`\n\nSix mutations failed their pins. Each restored fix passed again:\n\n- The complete old recognizer from `upstream/main`.\n- The old Z merge function.\n- The old radial merge function.\n- The original highest-mouth and through semantics.\n- The old mill detection filter from `upstream/main`.\n- Removal of the floor rim guard.\n\nThe complete old recognizer needed only the shared setter visibility after the module split.\nThe isolated merge mutations used the original functions from `upstream/main`.\n\nThe first quick gate found two existing through-hole regressions.\nThe floor rim guard resolves them:\n\n- `recognize_cross_finds_blind_and_through_radial_walls`\n- `recognize_cross_mixes_freely_with_the_z_pass`\n\nTargeted checks passed: 47 motion drilling tests, 9 app cross-drilling tests, and the app detection pin.\n\nValidation passed:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 39 steps, zero failures.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe pin reconstructs the reported dimensions with an original closed D50 bar and axis-aligned holes in vertical and horizontal orientations.\nWe did not exercise the original QA project, oblique-axis recognition, indexed drilling, or a machine run.\nThe existing mixed-list, plain-mill, and radial Z refusal checks remain in place.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes the expected files.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: Keep opposite blind holes separate and preserve their entry mouths during hole detection.\n\nFixes #2601\n",
